 - 2026-06-17: PHASE B3 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17) -- E3 EXECUTABLE-WORLD-MODEL solves of tr87 AND ft09, +1 level (L1) EACH, looped with a checkpoint per game + a hard per-game wall-time cap (breadth-of-progress beats an all-or-nothing single-game swing). Same harness as exp4327/exp4328 (arXiv:2605.05138; the codex agent induces + refines a Python world model per game, the Carnot WorldModelVerifier grounds it, plan_and_execute). Both are deep-tail games graph-explore NO-ADVANCEd (mechanic-limited); gpt-5.5 solved both in the SOTA paper. The codex agent IS the proposer (WRITES results/arc_e3/<game>/world_model.py per game; NO nested CodexProposer). HARD gate per game: offline_reproduced=true AND reproduced_levels>=1. An honest partial per game (best verifier_accuracy + the residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap) is PROGRESS. Report a per-game scorecard. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded ARC progress, NOT a moat). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; checkpoint after EACH game so a window-exhaustion preserves the first game's result. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete_e3_tr87_ft09_partial; results/experiment_4329_e3_executable_world_model_tr87_ft09.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE C (ARC NORTH STAR; shallow tail) -- adapter-free graph-explore DISCOVERY SWEEP over the remaining unsolved SHALLOW-tail games + reverse-engineer tn36's ACTION6 click-payload schema. The 2026-06-17 sweep cracked 7 games adapter-free (cd82/sp80/su15/tu93 + cn04/m0r0/sk48 via E1 salience+mask); 13 games remain unsolved. EXCLUDE the deep-tail E3 games (ar25/ka59/tr87/ft09 -- exp4327-4329 own those) and sc25 (provisional). SWEEP the shallow-tail candidates (bp35/dc22/g50t/lf52/re86/s5i5/sb26/vc33) with graph_explore_solve_v2/v3 (arXiv:2512.24156: salience-prioritized state-transition graph, shortest-path to untested state-action pairs) at the 12k DISCOVERY budget (per the budget finding: 12k is load-bearing for first-level discovery; do NOT inflate the +1-advance budget). RE tn36's ACTION6 data schema (it raises KeyError 'x' -- its click payload is NOT {{x,y}}; wrap clicks in tn36's expected payload before the explorer can advance it). CAPTURE + reproduction-gate any new L1 solves (arc_solver_kit.reproduce). Update ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml. Monotonic +1+: report reproducible_total_levels (>= the current 13, ideally more) + games_advanced. verifier_is_oracle=true (execution-grounded). An honest no-advance WITH exploration_actions_used>0 per game is COMPLETE and informs the next pick; capture the per-game dead-ends. NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: adapter_free_shallow_tail_no_advance_real_exploration_total13; results/experiment_4330_arc_adapter_free_discovery_sweep_shallow_tail.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE D (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; NEW mechanism = a LEARNED FRAME ENCODER) -- does a LEARNED frame encoder (vs the GENERIC grid features that nulled in exp4318) carry a game-invariant progress signal that transfers cross-game? .399 (exp4318) PROVED generic grid features (nonzero/colors/objects/spread/dominant) do NOT transfer cross-game (reduction ~1.0, positive control passed) and LOGGED a 'game-invariant ARC value representation' gap. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning experiment/milestone; re-measuring generic-feature transfer is churn. The NEW mechanism (the gap's candidate fix): train a small LEARNED frame ENCODER (a tiny CNN / learned feature map over raw frames, CPU) on the now-11 reproducibly-solved games' traces, producing a learned embedding the value-head consumes; re-test LEAVE-ONE-GAME-OUT cross-game search-efficiency transfer (does the learned-encoder value-head reduce OfflineSolver search states on a held-out game vs an untrained/uniform heuristic?). POSITIVE CONTROL: confirm the baseline solver solves the held-out level (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK guard). Report cross_game_state_reduction (held-out states_uniform / states_transferred) + per-held-out-game reads + a bootstrap CI95. Emit learned_encoder_transfer_helps BARE bool := (reduction > 1.0 AND CI95 lower bound > 1.0). verifier_is_oracle=false. A learned-encoder transfer where generic features failed CLOSES the gap (a richer game-invariant representation); a powered null SHARPENS the gap (the representation is still insufficient -> more solved games or a different encoder) and is decision-grade. NO TRM training; NO LLM weight mutation (the encoder + value-head are a tiny CPU heuristic over solver state). (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: learned_frame_encoder_transfer_no_improvement_positive_control_passed; results/experiment_4331_self_learning_learned_frame_encoder_cross_game_transfer.json
